  "caption": "Nephew Bo walks like a tiny ballerina, and the family chat has 47 opinions about why.\n\nToddler toe walking often fades on its own. What matters more is the pattern: when it started, whether one side is different, and whether heels can reach the floor. It isn't always a tight calf that needs stretching.\n\nWhat can help: checking whether your child can stand and squat with heels flat, noting when it started, barefoot play on varied surfaces, gentle cues with no shaming, and notes on milestones and family history for the clinician.\n\nGet it checked if it continues past about age 3, heels can't reach the floor, one side is worse, it began after normal walking, skills are lost, or falls are frequent.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
